  "note": "The room is in writing: The writer you picked writes the whole script.\n\nThe showrunner picked you in the audition. script.md holds your audition pages: keep their voice, and write the whole book.\n\nDrawability: Pages are drawn by an image model, one page per generation, from each character's and location's sheet, and a page drifts when it carries too much. So: at most 4 panels a page; at most 3 named characters in one panel; one location a page where the story allows (every new location needs its own sheet); no crowd that must be recognisable; a big moment gets a splash (one panel, the whole page). Count pages this way, not by comic convention. Every page you make keeps to it.\n\ndraft.md is the showrunner's own draft of the whole book. Write the book from it, in the voice of your audition pages: keep its structure, its scenes and the lines that work; fix what story.md, characters.md, world.md and facts.md contradict; make every page better than the draft's. Do not start over, and do not drop what it has unless the files require it.\n\nThe book is exactly 54 pages: pages 1-54, no more, no fewer.",
